# The module's own table, its words and settings. First: the other files will add to that table.
Combat.lua
# Its window: docked at the bottom middle, filling the screen from the middle half of the bottom edge
Window.lua
# The full screen's windows on Core's board: each registers itself (Board.Part); the talent planner seated
Board.lua
# Talents: our own window of your talents, as the game's (Talents/)
# Spellbook: our own window of your spells, as the game's (Book/)
# Where each entry stands on the pages, by the game's rules (lists in, lists out)
Book\Layout.lua
# What the book holds: the game's tabs, their spells as its book shows them, the search
Book\Data.lua
# One entry, as the game's: its icon and frame, name, rank, cooldown, the glow of a spell on no bar
Book\Item.lua
# The game's secure buttons over the icons, which cast out of a fight
Book\Casts.lua
# The book itself: its pages, tabs, the game's paging controls and settings
Book\Book.lua
# Your spellbook, pet book and talents keys opening ours (the game's override bindings; our keys: Bindings.xml)
Keys.lua
# A mark beside a creature's nameplate while it belongs to an objective of your quests still to do
QuestMarks.lua
